ene expression at the developing neuromuscular junction</article-title><source>Physiol Rev</source><year>1995</year><volume>75</volume><fpage>339</fpage><lpage>368</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7724666</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dugandzija-Novakovic</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Koszowski</surname><given-names>AG</given-names></name><name><surname>Levinson</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name><name><surname>Shrager</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Clustering of Na<sup>&#x0002b;</sup>channels and node of Ranvier formation in remyelinating axons</article-title><source>J Neurosci</source><year>1995</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>492</fpage><lpage>503</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7823157</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Flucher</surname><given-names>BE</given-names></name><name><surname>Daniels</surname><given-names>MP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Distribution of Na<sup>&#x0002b;</sup>channels and ankyrin in neuromuscular junctions is complementary to that of acetylcholine receptors and the 43 kd protein</article-title><source>Neuron</source><year>1989</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>163</fpage><lpage>175</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2560390</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gee</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name><name><surname>Madhaven</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Levinson</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name><name><surname>Caldwell</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name><name><surname>Sealock</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Froehner</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name></person-grou